  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Girinagar Police Station vs Suresh on 8 May, 2025 1 C.C.No.37139/2022 Kabc030872812022 In The Court Of The Xxxvii Addl.Chief Judicial Magistrate, Bangalore City. Dated this the 08th day of May, 2025. Present:Sri Syed Arfath Ibrahim M., B.A.L, L.L.B., Xxxvii Acjm., Bangalore. C.C. No.37139/2022 Judgment Under Sec.355 Of Cr.P.C., Complainant : State by Giri Nagara Police Station. Vs/- Accused : Suresh S/O Late Krishnappa Age 47 Years Manjunatha Lubricants And Electricls, Eeranna Gudde Circle, Banashanakri 3Rd Stage. Bengaluru City - 560 085. Date of offence : 26-08-2022",
    "facts": "** ** The Police-Sub-Inspector, Giri nagara Police Station has filed chargesheet against Accused for the offences punishable U/s. 3(1) (a),3(1)(b),3(1)(c)7(1)(a), 7(1)(b),4(1)(a),4(b),4(1)(c),4(1)(d),3(2)(3)(4)7(1) Girinagar Police Station vs Suresh on 8 May, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/198460357/ 1 (c) , 2000 and sec.285 of I.P.C. 2. The criminal law has been set into motion based on the first information statement of Deepak L. The gist of the prosecution case is that on 26-08-2022 the CW-1 received credible information and conducted raid along with CW 8 in the presence of CW 2 and 3 and found that the accused being the owner of Manjunatha Lubricants and Electrical shop situated at Eeranna Gudde circle, BSK 3rd stage without obtaining a valid license possessed Gas cylinders of various companies and the accused would refill small gas cylinders without adhering to safety measures and the accused with an intention to make wrongful gain had illegally stocked gas cylinders at sheet roof house at No. 69, 6 th Cross, 9th Main Road, Hrishikeshnagar, Hosakerehalli. It is further alleged that the accused had possessed gas cylinders unauthorisedly and was negligently filling gas cylinders with liquified petroleum gas and was unauthorizedly selling LPG in the market and he was also in 3 C.C.No.37139/2022 possession of LPG equipments. Based on the said information, a case in Cr.No.246/2022 came to be registered against the accused persons. 3. After completion of the investigation, the PSI of Giri Nagara P.S. has filed chargesheet against accused for the aforesaid offences. On receipt of charge sheet, this court took cognizance of the alleged offences. Pursuant to the issuance and service of summons, accused entered appearance and was enlarged on bail. Girinagar Police Station vs Suresh on 8 May, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/198460357/ 2 The prosecution papers was furnished to the accused as required U/s.207 of Cr.P.C. 4. The substance of accusation was read over to the accused in the language known to them, to which, the accused pleaded not guilty and submitted he has defence to make. The plea of the accused was recorded. Thereafter, the matter was set down for prosecution evidence. 5. In order to prove the charges, the prosecution has examined PW-1 to PW-4 and got marked Ex.P1 to Ex.P8 documents. The Statement of Accused as required U/s.313 of Cr.P.C. is recorded. In which, the accused has denied the 4 C.C.No.37139/2022 incriminating circumstances appeared against him. The accused has not let in either oral or documentary evidence on his behalf.",
